<title>MOROCCO: Morocco tourism earnings rise in 1996.</title>
<headline>Morocco tourism earnings rise in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moroccan Tourism Minister Mohamed Alaoui M'hamedi was quoted on Tuesday as saying that revenue from tourism were 11.5 billion dirhams ($1.26 billion) in 1996 compared to 9.9 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>M'hamedi, in an interview with Moroccan daily le Quotidien, said 1.65 million foreign tourists visited the North African country in 1996 compared to 1.52 million in 1995.</p>
</text>
